/**
 * CRISP Web Dashboard - Service Worker
 * ─────────────────────────────────────
 * Strategy:
 *   App files (HTML/JS/CSS) → Network-First (always get latest, cache as fallback)
 *   CDN assets              → Cache-First   (fonts, icons - rarely change)
 *   Static data (world.json)→ Cache-First   (large, never changes)
 *   API /api/v1/reports     → Stale-While-Revalidate (instant + background refresh)
 *   Everything else         → Network with cache fallback
 */

// v9/v8/v8/v11 → v10/v9/v9/v12 - Apr 2026 round-2 CSP fix.
// Bumping to evict any client that has stale HTML/CDN entries cached
// from the brief window where connect-src was missing tile hosts +
// the browser was heuristic-pinning the old CSP. Old SWs auto-replace
// because skipWaiting() runs in install + nginx now sends Cache-Control:
// no-cache on sw.js so the new code lands within seconds of deploy.
const APP_CACHE    = 'crisp-app-v155';  // v155 (Jun 2026): dashboard login - the authenticator (TOTP) code field is now OPTIONAL in the UI so accounts without 2FA (e.g. the UNDP demo/evaluator account) sign in on email + password only; MFA stays enforced server-side per account (mfa_enabled). create_admin.py gains --no-mfa. // v154 (Jun 2026): a LIVE op whose end-window has passed (ended_at < now) now badges ENDED - the backend matcher already refuses it new reports - and drops out of the live rail/summary into 'View all'; the idle-activity flag reads 'Quiet' (not 'Inactive') so it no longer contradicts a green LIVE badge; single live-vs-ended rule (CrispOpCard.isEffectivelyEnded) across badge + rail + registry. // v153 (Jun 2026): Active Operations rail - op cards show the FULL name + details (no truncation, wider identity column); dropped the RED/GREEN/AMBER health pill + mini-map radius icon in favour of a plain coverage radius (e.g. 30 Km); KPI chips re-spaced; the ops-summary MAP now stretches to match the left operations-list height. // v152 (Jun 2026): home AI assessment fills the row (full summary + key risks + resource needs + escalation); Recent Incidents feed shows REJECTED reports as Rejected (not Pending); analytics KPIs exclude rejected from pending/response/false-alarm rates. // v151 (Jun 2026): home - deleted Global Summary / Operational Impact / Executive Summary; relocated the Analytics dashboard OFF the header Tools into a 70/30 home section (70% analytics inline + 30% Recent Incidents feed, scrolls after 20) after Active Operations. // v150 (Jun 2026): home AI redesign - Situational Awareness panel REPLACED by the full-width global AI Assessment & Actions row (2-col: assessment | recommended actions, action bar full-width); Global Overview now two 50/50 equal-height columns (map | command centre) with the metric tiles stretching to fill the height. // v149 (Jun 2026): removed Building Intelligence from the home (buildings live only in the incident feed now). // v148 (Jun 2026): operation console redesign - removed LIVE/breadcrumb/exit row, vitals counts, operation map and buildings/reports worklist + Open-Incident-Feed; added op-scoped duplicate-review strip + 'View deployed crisis form'; kept AI command panel + actions + local conditions + exports. // v147 (Jun 2026): home batch - notification 'since last visit' watermark + queue destination, Section-N labels removed, AI panel fixed height, compact command-centre cards, AI action bar (reject/notify/false-alarm/merge), AI re-run staleness + input-hash cache + graceful degradation, duplicate-checks strip. // v146 (Jun 2026): pre-deploy review fixes - Situational Awareness "Where" facet now derives from the live operations the rail loaded (the /analytics/assess payload carries no top_operations, so it was always empty); escalation_likelihood {level,rationale} was rendered as the literal "[object Object]" - now shows the level (rationale tooltip). // v145 (Jun 2026): status-tab row CSS - the 4 tabs (Pending/Responding/Resolved/Rejected) now stay a TIGHT left-grouped segmented cluster (flex:0 0 auto + justify-content:flex-start + tighter padding) instead of stretching edge-to-edge across the narrower feed header. // v144 (Jun 2026): fix 'clicking one incident expands every building'. ROOT CAUSE: _mountClusterWindow force-open (building/triage/queue scope) did _expandedClusters.add(key) for EVERY cluster, permanently polluting the persistent Set, so afterwards every building rendered expanded in all views (and selecting an incident re-rendered, revealing it). FIX: force-open is now render-only (_renderClusterCard(c, forceOpen)) - never written to _expandedClusters; the header toggle reads the visual collapsed-state so a force-opened card still collapses on first click. // v143 (Jun 2026): count-consistency follow-through - loaded-path Critical badge counts OPEN critical only (was incl. resolved-criticals at small scale); counts.resolved now = RESOLVED+FALSE_ALARM (matches the feed's Resolved tab via _statusTabFor) so tabs partition the total exactly. // v142 (Jun 2026): COUNT CONSISTENCY - one source of truth across the home Command Centre, the incidents-page tabs/header, the deep-linked queues and the rendered feed. A REJECTED report is set aside (Rejected count only) + excluded from every open/active/critical count (backend analytics.py active filter + crisis_forms per-op critical/unattended/needs_review + frontend updateCommandStats + _applyQueueFilter already did). Fixes 'Critical says 2 but the queue is empty' (a rejected report was counted as an open critical). Header total + home Total tile now BOTH show total REPORTS (was incidents-entities vs reports - they disagreed). New counts.pending (status PENDING, not rejected) drives both the home Review-pending tile and the incidents Pending tab. // v141 (Jun 2026): final long-feed auto-scroll fix (crisp-nav.js) - drive host.scrollTop to the VIEWPORT centre (was scrollIntoView block:center, which centres in the feed scrollport that extends past the fold -> far-down card rested at ratio 0.475); dropped the scrollTop>8 re-assert guard that short-circuited far-down corrections; settle window 2.5s -> 6.5s to outlast the 4s feed poll's list rebuild. Verified 40+ flake-free runs + 35-operations 18/18 + nav/scroll regression 15/15. // v140 (Jun 2026): incident-feed fixes - (1) Collapse-all now works in the op-grouped GLOBAL feed: _clusterApplyAll also collapses/expands the OPERATION sections (.opg-op), not just the already-collapsed building cards (was a no-op); (2) feed panel + right detail/operation-console panels narrowed ~20% (operator request); (3) long-feed auto-scroll past the 50-card limit re-asserts the scroll across progressive-reveal re-renders (crisp-nav.js revealSelected RAF re-centre loop + MutationObserver) so the selected card lands comfortably in view (fixes 35-operations:382 without breaking the siblings). // v139 (Jun 2026): Command Centre fixes - (1) headline tile = Total REPORTS (superset) not deduped incidents, so it's never smaller than its Resolved/Rejected/Review-pending buckets; (2) replaced the Affected-countries tile with a Review-pending tile (queue=needs-review); (3) AI assessment NO LONGER auto-runs on load - click-only (Analyze Global); (4) removed the duplicate metric chips under the global AI panel (the Command Centre tiles are the single source; they had used a different aggregate so looked mismatched); Situational Awareness shows a click-to-generate CTA until the assessment is run. // v138 (Jun 2026): home restructure - 3 labelled sections (Global Overview map/command-centre-tiles/AI panel, Situational Awareness AI facets, Active Operations rail led by +New with per-op Buildings/Resolved/Rejected, Global Summary + Executive summary); AI assessment auto-runs on load; new analytics aggregates. // v137 (Jun 2026): incident-card declutter - DROP the severity TEXT badge (the left colour strip already carries severity), the status pill ('Needs review' - redundant inside a status tab), and the Notify button (it's on hover + the detail panel). KEEP the severity strip, title, channel/source icon (added the missing RN/Android .qrt-src-android colour), confidence chip. Location now shows FULLY (no ellipsis; meta row wraps). The left feed bar is wider (clamp(460,31vw,580); responsive 440/380). // v136 (Jun 2026): building-tag follow-ups - (1) the Rejected status tab no longer clips off the right edge of a narrow feed panel: .feed-tablist takes its own full row + wraps (was inline-flex/nowrap). (2) free-text leak fix - the incident PDF 'Building / structure' row, the dossier-PDF row, and the per-incident AI /ai-assess 'Name:' now use the GATED canonical building name (new Report.display_building_name SSOT property): a free-text 'what was hit' answer is shown clearly flagged 'unverified', never AS the building name; exports gain a canonical building_name column (raw infrastructure_name + infra_name_from_osm kept). // v135 (Jun 2026): building-tag consistency - the Building Console header now uses the SAME _taggedBuildingName gate as the Incident Feed (no more raw free-text 'what was hit' shown as the building name in the Console while the feed shows 'Unnamed building'); its empty fallback collapses 'Untitled building' -> 'Unmapped building'. Pairs with the PWA from_osm capture fix (v357) + the 0063 heal migration so an explicitly tagged building shows ONE canonical name everywhere. // v134 (Jun 2026): GLOBAL feed shows the full Operation -> Building -> Incident hierarchy. When real operations exist, renderClusterFeed groups the rich .cc-cluster building cards under their Operation via _mountOpGroupedClusters (reuses .opg-op header/rail + _renderClusterCard; _clusterSummary gains opId = dominant crisis_event_id). Unassigned buildings -> a 'no operation' section. Op/building-scoped views + all-unassigned data stay the flat building list. Ops expanded, buildings collapsed by default; View-> opens the operation summary. // v133 (Jun 2026): Incident Feed GRADUATES to the real incidents entity (Building -> Incident -> Report). The feed stays report-sourced (map/search/filters/export/status untouched) but groups loaded reports by the server-assigned incident_id (_groupByIncident): a single-report incident renders as before; a multi-report incident renders ONE lead card with an 'N reports' expander (toggleIncidentMembers -> GET /incidents/{id} members, falls back to the locally grouped members / report duplicates). Building + op counts = distinct incident units (_distinctIncidents); the scope banner reads the REAL analytics counts.incidents (now COUNT(DISTINCT incident_id) + incident-less singletons, server-scoped). Clicking a multi-report card opens the Incident Detail. Subsumes the v132 duplicate chip/expander. // v132 (Jun 2026): Incident Feed clean 3-colour hierarchy - Operations & Buildings become lightweight HEADER ROWS (drop card border/background; only the Incident card keeps a surface); ONE connector (parent-coloured rail + ::before elbow, incident elbow slate->teal); emerald active-ring -> teal left-accent; sky-blue dup badge + blue drill link -> neutral. Single metric: building header shows the MERGED incident count + a neutral 'N duplicates' chip (was 'N incidents . M reports'); _dualCount drops the reports half; the per-card duplicates badge is now an EXPANDER revealing the merged duplicates NESTED + dimmed under the primary (GET /{id}/duplicates, confirmed). // v124 (Jun 2026): Building Console consolidation - the competing metrics (the 5-score Intelligence grid + humanitarian_priority 'Why this priority', the separate AI-assessment card, the standalone satellite score, and the old building_confidence card) are REPLACED by ONE Building RISK Score using the EXACT incident .dp-assess card + breakdown UX. The combined act-first score (severity 30 + incident-assessments 25 + corroboration 20 + evidence 15 + recency 10 = 100, high=urgent/red) is computed by services/building_risk.py from the constituent incident credibility scores; the breakdown modal decomposes the 5 weighted factors + lists the contributing incidents (click->open). migration 0062. humanitarian_priority still sorts the hot-list in the backend. // v123 (Jun 2026): duplicate-review relocation - the global "Buildings needing duplicate review" awareness PANEL is REMOVED from the top of the feed; instead each building ROW in the building-grouped feed shows a per-building dup-count badge (.cc-cluster-dup, candidate_pairs + N high, from /reports/buildings-needing-review ingested into _dupReviewMap + painted after the rows render) that opens the building console where the Potential-Duplicates merge controls live; the Operations summary page keeps its "N buildings need duplicate review" chip. // v122 (Jun 2026): Command Center - a consistent decision+action panel (CrispCommandPanel) at Global + Operation: AI 'Analyze' (aggregate child confidence + ONE claude-sonnet-4-6 synthesis -> situation/risks/escalation/recommended-actions/priority/resources) whose recommended actions are EXECUTABLE one-click cascades; and a SCOPED ACTION BAR backed by a new set-based cascade engine (POST /operations/{id}/cascade/{action} + /reports/cascade global filtered slice, admin) that percolates an action to every incident+report in the slice in ONE transaction (scale-safe to 500k reports), with a blast-radius dry-run confirm, reason-gated destructive actions, bounded responder notify, single audit row + Undo (/reports/cascade-revert). Building keeps its A2 console cascade. migrations 0061 (cascade_action_log + scope_assessment). // v121 (Jun 2026): usability + security batch - (A1) hard-purge step-up is TOTP-only in production (password fallback rejected; dev mock code for tests); (A3) device-vs-submitted location mismatch (>1km) is surfaced to the AI dossier + credibility location REASON text + exports (device lat/lng columns) WITHOUT changing any credibility number; (A4) Operations cards/banners de-duplicated (4-chip KPI strip, merged health.status pill + unattended flag, verified/new-24h moved to detail); (A5) operation-level actions (Edit Form / View Config / Export Reports / Download Summary PDF) + a new multi-section Operation PDF; (A2) the Building Console is a flat collapsible dp-section stack in the incident-detail visual language (Overview/Intelligence tabs retired) + the deep-link incident reveal switches lifecycle tabs so a RESPONDING/RESOLVED incident scrolls into view. // v120 (Jun 2026): bug-fix batch - (B1) the impact-assessment (electricity/health/needs) questions in the pack builder + wizard are now generic, freely-toggleable blocks (removed the UNDP compliance warning banner + UNDP tags/Appendix-1 framing); (B3) a Pending/Responding/Resolved incident-feed status tab whose bucket is 0 is muted + non-clickable (.feed-tab.tab-empty); (B4) the incident PDF + all GIS exports now include the crisis-pack form_data answers with resolved labels (added the backend PDF Crisis-Pack Answers row + upgraded the client incident PDF to verbatim labels via ensurePackSchema). // v119 (Jun 2026): UNDP Appendix-1 mandatory questions via the crisis-form pack (admin + dashboard). The pack BUILDER (cc-crisis.js) + Start-New-Operation WIZARD (cc-wizard.js) gain the 3 UNDP questions (electricity/health/pressing-needs) as individual, default-ON, options-locked catalog blocks with a non-blocking compliance hint when toggled off; buildSchema stamps explicit per-field channels (UNDP=APP/ANDROID/WHATSAPP/TELEGRAM, else App-only). The incident-detail 'Crisis-pack answers' section re-renders with VERBATIM question + option labels once the pack schema loads (ensurePackSchema), not raw codes. // v118 (Jun 2026): hierarchy + image-tag consistency (P1, frontend) - the Global > Operation > Building > Incident spine is now UNIFORM on every lineage surface: the incident-detail breadcrumb + building console + op-dashboard banner + incident PDF show all levels with muted 'No operation'/'Unmapped building' placeholders instead of silently dropping them (was 'Global > Incident > #id'); op banner uses 'Global > {op}' not 'CRISP / Operations /'. Building NAMES on images/feeds/breadcrumbs (lightbox geo-overlay, scope-bar crumb, nearby modal, cluster name) now come from the OSM record only (_taggedBuildingName) - never the reporter's free-text 'what was hit'. // v117 (Jun 2026): Building Console resilience - bounded fetch (15s AbortController) + a recoverable error state with Retry instead of an endless 'Loading building...' spinner when GET /buildings/{id} fails/times out or the render throws; stale-click guard. // v116 (Jun 2026): Incident Feed redesign - breadcrumb header (Global > Operation + Switch) replaces the title + standalone context card; click a building to expand its incidents AND open its console (single-open accordion); totals (N incidents - M reports) folded into the status-tab row; opt-in Compact density (crisp_feed_density); building-list infinite scroll (10/page). // v115 (Jun 2026): redundancy sweep - Building Console incident rows lead with the crisis type (not the building-name-bearing inc.title); removed the dead building-name-first _cardTitle helper. // v114 (Jun 2026): post-review fixes - title-attribute XSS escape (escapeAttr) on the incident card, building cascade reopen un-sticks a notified building (RESPONDING->ACTIVE), assess never-fatal on a per-incident failure, single-report export of a rejected report no longer empty. // v113 (Jun 2026): Building as a first-class operational entity. The Building Console gains a Building Assessment card + workspace (Run Building Assessment runs the per-incident AI assessment across the building's non-duplicate incidents and consolidates a building confidence roll-up + per-incident breakdown), a standalone Assessment Report PDF, and a state-machine ACTIONS group mirroring the incident actions (Notify Response Team / Resolve / False Alarm / Reject / Reopen) that CASCADE to the building's incidents + their reports in one audited, reversible batch. Building 'Reject' cascades verdict REJECTED to all reports; the export path now excludes rejected reports (must-have #11). Backend: POST /buildings/{id}/assess, POST /buildings/{id}/cascade/{action}, GET /buildings/{id}/assessment.pdf; migration 0060 (building_assessments). Also folds the v112 review fixes: building-console op-scope survives in-console actions, the building-name cluster link is a keyboard/SR-accessible button, export since is queue-guarded. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v112 (Jun 2026): Building-name + console-scope fixes + v111-review remediation. Building clusters/cards/console now name a building by its TAG (OSM footprint name) disambiguated with the area ('DoubleTree Hotel · Koramangala') - NEVER the infrastructure_type ('Commercial'/'Government'/'Transport communication' was the mis-naming). Clicking a building NAME opens the summary console (the duplicate open-icon was removed; the chevron still expands inline). The console op-scopes its incident LIST to the active operation (global = all reports; header roll-up stays building-wide). v111-review fixes: exports now follow the active status TAB (was frozen at PENDING,VERIFIED - must-have #11); the queue-grouped feed honours Critical/search/chips/crisis-drill; status tabs are neutralized when a queue owns the population; tab/Critical labels + filter/sort aria are i18n-wired (must-have #2); ARIA tablist holds only the 3 tabs; banner + search counts exclude rejected. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v111 (Jun 2026): Incident Feed simplification - the feed panel collapses to TWO rows: (row 1) a single clickable breadcrumb (Global > Operation > Building) with the Total folded inline, plus ONE "Switch" button that toggles between operations & global (its menu lists Global + every operation); (row 2) three status TABS - Pending / Responding / Resolved (renamed from "Needs Action" for consistency) - each with an inline count, that show the status's incidents GROUPED BY BUILDING on click. Critical is a cross-cutting quick-filter chip; Filters + Sort are two small icons (Filters opens a popover that now also holds the Rejected entry). Retired: the Buildings/All-Incidents view toggle, the 4-pill KPI strip, the standalone Global/Rejected banner buttons, and the flat NEEDS ACTION/RESPONDING/CLOSED list (renderTriageQueue). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v110 (Jun 2026): incident-detail Actions are now a STATE MACHINE - a settled report only offers the REVERSAL of its current decision, never a fresh Reject/Delete. REJECTED (verdict) → "Rejected" banner + Revert decision (PATCH /review {NOT_REVIEWED}); RESPONDING/notified → "Response team notified" banner + Mark Resolved / Mark as False Alarm / Revert (no Reject/Delete - the notice already went out, a false alarm is the follow-up); RESOLVED/FALSE_ALARM → status banner + Reopen; OPEN (PENDING) → Notify Response Team + Reject + Delete. Backend: NEW PATCH /reports/{id}/reopen (RESPONDING/RESOLVED/FALSE_ALARM → PENDING, clears dispatch/arrival ts) + reverse transitions added to _REPORT_STATUS_TRANSITIONS; revertRejection/reopenReport in app.js merge the out-of-feed detail cache too. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v109 (Jun 2026): Home→Incident navigation clarity ("where am I / how did I get here"). (1) Global Monitoring: dropped the "Global Attention" label so the right-side cards align top+bottom with the map. (2) BUILDING + TRIAGE are now first-class FEED SCOPES on the Operation axis - client-side filters (no refetch) layered on the op/global set: #/incidents;bld=<id> scopes to a building, #/incidents;op=none = the "not in any operation" triage bucket (setBuildingScope/setTriageScope/_applyScopeFilter in app.js; router parses op=none + bld=). (3) The #queue-banner is now a clickable BREADCRUMB SPINE Global › [Operation|Triage] › [Building] (each crumb steps up) + the category as a clearable chip - the always-on "where am I" surface. (4) Clicking a Global Attention card lands on a feed GROUPED by Operation → Building (renderOperationGroupedFeed; collapsible sections + Triage/No-building buckets; headers drill the scope). (5) The incident-detail Building breadcrumb now SCOPES the feed (setBuildingScope) instead of popping the console (the console stays behind its own button). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/router.js/cc-home.js + styles.css. // v108 (Jun 2026): Home page redesign - GLOBAL MONITORING moved to the TOP (map + Global Attention), then ACTIVE OPERATIONS as a width-matched split that mirrors the Global Monitoring grid: the most-recent 5 operations as COMFORTABLE cards (the same CrispOpCard the /operations page uses) on the LEFT, and an Operations Summary column on the RIGHT (the portfolio count chips + orphan-critical alert + a NEW single all-operations hotspot map #cc-ops-map with one number-tagged marker per operation = critical count, colour = health, click → that operation). Building/Operational Intelligence stays below. cc-home.js renderOpsRail split across #cc-ops-rail (cards) + #cc-ops-summary (chips) + renderOpsMap; reuses the .cc-split 1.6fr/1fr grid so the two rows' column widths line up. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale cc-home.js. // v107 (Jun 2026): Building-centric Incident Feed Phase 2E - first-class INCIDENT entity surfaced in the dashboard. NEW window.openIncidentDetail(incidentId) renders an Incident Detail overlay (separate from selectReport so the tested report-detail flow is untouched): incident info + status/severity pills, lifecycle controls (PATCH status/severity), member-report list (each opens its report), per-report Split, and Merge-into-sibling - all backed by the Phase-2 /api/v1/incidents endpoints (GET list/detail, POST merge/move-report/split-report, PATCH). Reachable via the ?incidentDetail=<id> deep-link on /incidents (router). Pairs with the Phase-2 BACKEND: incidents table (migration 0058) + reports.incident_id, intake HIGH-join assignment across all 6 channels, the 0059 backfill of legacy reports, and incident_id threaded through ReportResponse + every export format. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/router.js. // v106 (Jun 2026): Building-centric Incident Feed (Phase 1). The dashboard feed now defaults to a BUILDINGS view (Global → Operations → Buildings → Incidents → Reports) with a flat "All Incidents" toggle; the Building Console is a lean 3-zone workspace (Summary / Reports / Duplicate review + an Intelligence tab); the operation dashboard gains a roll-up line (N incidents · M reports · 🔗 K buildings need duplicate review · U unreviewed) whose dup-review chip drills into the op's Buildings worklist; the GLOBAL "Potential Duplicates / Merge all" panel is replaced by a READ-ONLY "Buildings needing duplicate review" awareness card (merge lives ONLY in the building/operation workspace, never global) consuming GET /reports/buildings-needing-review; the feed-card "🔗 N duplicate reports" merged badge is now ACTIONABLE (role=button → openBuildingConsole) when the report is building-tagged. ROUTER: an /incidents deep-link carrying ?incident=<id> OR a ;queue=<key> state-seg forces the flat QUEUE view (transient, not persisted) so the targeted/queue-filtered cards are revealable + highlightable (the building-grouped default hides them in collapsed sections). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/cc-operations.js/router.js/crisp-building-card.js + styles.css. // v105 (Jun 2026): R6 deferred-upload visibility - a non-SMALL tier the CLIENT deliberately deferred (bandwidth_tier_deferred = slow network, OR the new storage_evicted = shed under device storage pressure after the SMALL preview delivered) is classified 'delayed' (retryable / awaiting connectivity) NOT 'lost' in _classifyHighTier, and a distinct amber "Original (deferred - storage)" chip renders for storage_evicted. Pairs with the PWA indefinite-retention + smart-eviction change (no more silent 30-day expiry). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v104 (Jun 2026): only a GENUINELY OSM-tagged building (new _taggedBuildingName: building_id + infrastructure_name + infrastructure_name_from_osm !== false) is shown as a building NAME + Building Console link. The "Other / not listed" free-text "what was hit" label (infrastructure_name_from_osm === false) was being coords-attached to a building_id and rendered as the building name with a console route in BOTH the feed card title AND the detail "Location & Building" row + breadcrumb. Now that free-text shows as the incident TITLE text only (never a building link); the detail building row + breadcrumb segment render only for tagged buildings (or genuine needs_manual_mapping typed names). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v103 (Jun 2026): feed card - the building-tagged TITLE (building name) IS now the Building Console link (building icon + hover cue); removed the separate generic "🏢 Console" link from the location row so the building name appears once and is itself the clickable console affordance. Card-body click still opens the incident (title onclick stops propagation). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v102 (Jun 2026): reporter TIER restored as a calm always-visible chip in the incident detail (dp-reporter-tier, data-tier + emoji/label from CRISP_TIERS_BY_ID). v86 had moved reporter trust to the Assessment "Reporter" segment, but that segment is gated on a server-computed credibility pass - so an un-assessed report showed NO reporter tier, regressing the UNDP "reporter_tier must surface" field (audit finding #3 / e2e 08-v4-field-parity). The credibility SCORE still lives only in the Assessment; only the tier label returns. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v101 (Jun 2026): Incident Feed brought into PARITY with the incident workflow - the feed card now shows the composite Confidence Score + band (shared _confidenceChip; replaced the satellite-sub-score evidence chip), a verdict-aware status pill + "Notify Responders" CTA (shared _displayStatus/_cardActionEl; replaced "SEND HELP"/"HELPED"/"Help Sent"; REJECTED incidents render no live CTA - fixes the rejected-queue bug), the BUILDING name as the card title + Console deep-link when building-tagged, and split media icons. Tree-view rows + the hover fast-preview route through the same helpers. Feed chrome: KPI "Helped"->"Responding"; the "Verified" filter now means composite band (VERIFIED/LIKELY) not raw satellite>=60; new "Needs review" filter chip (chip_needs_review x6 langs); confidence sort = composite incident_credibility.score. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v100 (Jun 2026): incident breadcrumb restored to the FULL operational hierarchy - Global › [Operation] › [Building] › #incident. The building segment (dropped in v84/v88) is back: when r.building_id is set it shows r.infrastructure_name (or "Building") and links to the Building Console (openBuildingConsole); the operation segment shows when r.crisis_event_id is set. Both optional, so an unassigned no-building report is still "Global › #id". (The building also still appears in the Location & Building section - the crumb is the nav spine.) selectReport _bc builder now composes _gSeg + _opSeg + _bldgSeg + _idSeg. e2e 42 breadcrumb test re-pointed (asserts .dp-bc-bldg present); 38 unaffected (substring matches). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v99 (Jun 2026): Actions section SIMPLIFIED for least cognitive load. The action surface is now ONE state-aware primary (Notify Response Team / Mark Resolved / Resolved) + exactly two buttons: Reject and Delete. "Notify Response Team" is now a one-click DUMMY responder set - it always PATCHes /dispatch (→ RESPONDING + reporter PWA push), no responder-selection modal (openNotifyModal/notify-responders left defined but unwired). DROPPED from the panel: the verdict dropdown (Accept/Reject/False-alarm), Mark dispatched / Mark on-site chips, the lives counter, the overflow menu, and the whole _renderReviewerActions strip. Reject + Delete are now top-level outline buttons (warn/danger) that open the existing reason-required confirm modals. Export kept but quieted (neutral, not red). New clean CSS .dp-actions/.dp-act-primary/.dp-act-respond/.dp-act-2. e2e 03 reviewer-workflow re-pointed to the API (verdict/timestamps UI gone); 49-actions rewritten for the one-click notify + button-driven reject/delete. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v98 (Jun 2026): Actions section redesign (core). (1) "Send Help" → "Notify Response Team": opens a modal (openNotifyModal) listing responders linked to the incident's building+operation (GET /reports/{id}/responders), multi-select + SMS/Email channels (channel auto-detected from the single responder_contact: '@'=email else SMS), "Notify responders" → POST /reports/{id}/notify-responders (sends SMS via Twilio / Email via SMTP, audits REPORT_NOTIFY_RESPONDERS, moves to Active Response/RESPONDING, pushes the reporter). Empty state links to Building Console + "Mark responding anyway". (2) Reject: prompt() replaced by a proper confirm modal (openRejectModal) with a required reason textarea; rejected reports are now HIDDEN from the active feed + every queue (_applyQueueFilter) and reachable ONLY via the new 'rejected' queue + a "🚫 Rejected (N)" entry in the context banner. (3) Delete: confirm() replaced by a high-severity modal (openDeleteModal) with a required reason → DELETE /reports/{id}?reason= → stored on DeletionAuditLog.deletion_reason (migration 0057) + audit details. Shared _crispActionModal helper. NOTE: SMS works in prod (Twilio); SMTP/email is NOT configured in prod (graceful no-op, reported honestly). DEFERRED: responder→system feedback loop (responder-facing portal). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v97 (Jun 2026): "Re-run assessment" moved OFF the Confidence Score card INTO the breakdown workspace - the card's full-width .dp-assess-rerun button is removed (card is now just the score + contributors + "View breakdown"); re-run lives as the modal's sticky-header "Re-run assessment" button (always reachable while scrolling the breakdown). runFullAssessment's spinner-button lookup now also targets the modal's .assess-rerun-top. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v96 (Jun 2026): (a) the incident History/activity section is now OPEN by default (always visible on scroll, not collapsed). (b) "Incident PDF" export rebuilt to capture 100% of the data section-by-section, A4 portrait + printable: window.exportPDF is now async - fetches the FULL report by id + the audit trail (/audit?limit=50) + duplicate candidates, embeds every image (highest-quality complete photo variant + satellite) as a data: URI so they print at full quality with no load race, and renders 13 sections (Overview · Confidence assessment w/ per-check breakdown + equation · AI dossier · Satellite verification · Location & building · Description/transcript · Crisis-pack answers · Service status · Evidence & metadata checks · Corroboration & duplicates · Visual evidence · Media summary · History & audit trail). @page size:A4 portrait + break-inside:avoid sections + object-fit:contain images. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v95 (Jun 2026): the Confidence Score is now the SINGLE investigative workspace for ALL automated validation. (1) Clicking the score opens a 5-section breakdown - Score composition · Satellite verification (FULLY EMBEDDED: imagery + a ground↔satellite wipe comparison + the 4 sub-scores + AI observations + re-verify) · Duplicate analysis (lazy GET /reports/{id}/duplicates + nearby-within-5km fallback, with distance/similarity/open-related) · Evidence & metadata checks (REAL signals only - GPS device-vs-edited consistency, geocoding confidence, capture-vs-receipt timestamps, checksum/PII-blur status, AI photo analysis; NO fabricated "authenticity" verdict since the codebase has no tamper/EXIF analyzer) · AI reasoning. The operator never leaves the assessment to review satellite/duplicate evidence. (2) The satellite gauge/result + the Photo/Satellite/Compare view-toggle were REMOVED from the Evidence section (citizen photo + audio stay there); the inline #dp-duplicates panel section was removed (it lives in the modal now). (3) The Confidence Score CARD adds a contributor checklist (AI/Satellite/Location/Duplicates/Reporter ✓) + "Last assessed N ago" (server assessed_at = verification.scored_at, else the client run-time cache). (4) BUG FIX: reopening the breakdown no longer asks to re-run - _applyReportData's poll-merge now preserves prior fields ({...prev,...r,...geo}) so a transient null incident_credibility can't wipe the assessed state, AND a per-session __assessCache snapshots the result against the report id; the modal/card reuse it. Re-run is the only fresh-analysis trigger. Backend incident_credibility gains assessed_at. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v94 (Jun 2026): Report Assessment is now ONE system-only Confidence Score (0-100). The scattered "Human Reporter / AI / Satellite / Dedup" signal bar + the separate "Run satellite check" + "Run AI assessment" CTAs are replaced by a SINGLE primary CTA "AI-Assisted Report Assessment" (runFullAssessment) that runs every automated check (AI content + satellite) in the background, then the server-computed credibility (services/credibility.py, now PURE-MACHINE ADDITIVE: AI 30 + Satellite 25 + Location 15 + Corroboration 15 + Reporter 15 = 100) renders as one clickable score. Clicking the score opens a breakdown modal (.assess-modal) explaining each check - ran?, points awarded / max, evidence - plus the exact summation and the methodology. CRITICAL: the score is the system's automated assessment ONLY; a human accept/reject verdict NO LONGER moves it (the old supreme-override ACCEPTED->100 / REJECTED->0 is removed) - the verdict is the operational status, shown separately. The dead Evidence "Run verification" empty-state CTA (_renderVerifyEmptyCTA) was removed. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v93 (Jun 2026): wider incident detail panel + attributes inline. The panel width is now clamp(420px, 40vw, 560px) (was 380px) so more fits with minimal scroll, capped so it never dominates a small screen. The "Attributes" collapsed accordion is gone - the calm attribute chips (crisis type / damage / debris / services / reporter / crisis-form) are an always-visible chip row in the Summary glance (the extra width gives them room without clutter); crisis-pack answers stay a collapsed accordion in the Details zone. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v92 (Jun 2026): History accordion no longer nests a redundant "Timeline" accordion inside it - _renderIncidentTimeline now returns the timeline rows directly (it's only used inside the History section), so History shows the lifecycle events + the admin audit ribbon flat, no accordion-in-an-accordion. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v91 (Jun 2026): duplicate management consolidated to the BUILDING level. The incident detail's "Possible duplicates" section is now READ-ONLY - the inline merge DECISIONS (Merge / Not-dup / Set-primary / Remove / Unmerge-all) are removed; instead it shows the corroborating reports + the white-box "why" reasons (evidence from each merged report stays one click away via the report link) and a single "Review & merge in Building Console" link that routes to openBuildingConsole(building_id), where the merge workflow lives. Single source of truth = the primary report; each merged report's unique evidence remains accessible. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v90 (Jun 2026): Location & Building row - the building NAME is now itself the clickable link to the Building Console (the separate "Console" button is removed - less clutter); the per-report "V N of M · Older" building-version ribbon is removed from the incident detail (version/duplicate state is a BUILDING-level concern, surfaced in the Building Console reached via the building name). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v89 (Jun 2026): the nearby-incidents modal now GROUPS incidents by BUILDING (Building › Incident, groups open by default). Each building header shows the building name + incident count + nearest distance and opens the Building Console on click; incidents nest beneath, each opening that incident; reports with no mapped building fall into a "Not in a mapped building" group. (Merged-away duplicates remain excluded - sourced from the feed working set.) Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v88 (Jun 2026): incident breadcrumb + nearby CTA. Breadcrumb is now "Global › {Operation name} › #{report id}" - the redundant standalone "Operations" segment is dropped and the final segment is the incident's own short report id (was the generic word "Incident"). The "N more reports nearby" chip is now a CTA that opens a modal listing the nearby incidents (severity dot + type + place + status + distance), each click-through to that incident; the list is sourced from the feed working set which already EXCLUDES merged-away duplicates, so a primary never lists the reports merged under it. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v87 (Jun 2026): Incident UX pass 2 - hierarchy/accordions/actions. UX-E: the Timeline + Activity Log accordions merged into ONE "History" accordion (lifecycle timeline + admin audit ribbon - both chronological). UX-G: the attribute chips + service lifelines collapse into a named "Attributes" accordion in the Details zone BELOW the Assessment (via flex order) - the reference chips no longer clutter the top glance; crisis-pack answers sit alongside it. UX-H: the redundant "Export PDF" was removed from the action overflow (export is grouped once in the dedicated Export menu). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v86 (Jun 2026): Incident UX cognitive-load pass 2. UX-C: the duplicate satellite "Run verification" CTA was removed from Evidence - the satellite-run trigger lives once in the Incident Assessment ("Run satellite check"); the standalone reporter-TIER chip was removed (reporter trust shows once in the Assessment Reporter segment). UX-F: attribute chips (crisis type / damage / debris / reporter / crisis-form) are calm-neutral - saturated colour is reserved for the two decision signals (severity badge + credibility band). UX-D: the image quality-tier switcher reveals on hover (was a permanent fixture) + the "PII Protected" badge is quietened. UX-I: a single-incident Export menu (Incident PDF · Evidence ZIP · GeoJSON · KML · CSV, scoped via ?report_id=) replaces the two loose export icons; the aggregate formats (Sitrep / Analytics / Shapefile / Data dictionary) are hidden behind an "Open full Export Center" link. Backend: _fetch_export_rows gains an optional report_id filter (csv/geojson/kml/count). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v85 (Jun 2026): Incident header dedup-2. UX-A: the status pill carries the age ("Needs review · 42m ago"); removed the separate header time badge AND the "Waiting Xm" urgency chip (the same fact was shown three ways). UX-B: the channel badge IS the source entry-point - clicking it opens a popover (full channel name + Report ID with copy + media received + absolute submitted time), replacing the standalone "Source Details" collapsible section. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v84 (Jun 2026): Incident Details full-page DEDUP - every fact appears exactly once. Removed the duplicate headline (type lived in the header title + the headline; place name lived in the headline while the Location box showed only coords); the breadcrumb is now pure scope nav (Global/Operation/Incident, no building segment); a single "Location & Building" section owns everything spatial - place NAME + COORDS shown together, plus a building sub-row (infrastructure_name + needs-mapping + version + one "Console" button) - so infrastructure_name / Building-history / version no longer also appear as chips; the chip row holds incident attributes only; and the redundant reviewer-actions verdict chip is gone (the header combined status states it). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v83 (Jun 2026): Incident Details redesign - one decision stack. The detail panel is re-presented into mutually-exclusive sections: the header is identity-only (severity shows ONCE on its badge, not echoed in the headline + a urgency chip; the operational status + the review verdict are MERGED into ONE combined status pill - _displayStatus: Needs review -> Accepted/Rejected -> Responding -> Resolved - instead of two competing "PENDING" + "Not reviewed" pills); ALL evaluation collapses into ONE "Incident Assessment" section - a single backend-computed Incident Credibility Score (services/credibility.py: strong human override, machine blend, honest UNVERIFIED suppression) with a 5-signal contribution bar + an in-place breakdown (human/AI/satellite/reporter/dedup), replacing the scattered "Credibility Check" button + raw AI row. The body is a flex column re-ordered into Header -> Summary -> Evidence (photos+audio always visible) -> Assessment -> Activity -> sticky Actions. Backend also drops dead/stub data (AIAnalysis fabricated damage_score/detected_labels/ai_severity/processing_time_ms + legacy cluster tables, migration 0056) and persists reviewer identity (reviewed_by, migration 0055). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v82 (Jun 2026): reverse-geocode no longer double-hits a dead provider. The feed place-name lookup (reverseGeocode) called geocode.maps.co FIRST, but that provider REQUIRES an API key we do not ship - every call returned 401 and fell straight through to the OpenStreetMap Nominatim fallback, so the dashboard made TWO upstream requests per report (one always-doomed) for one result (~60 wasted 401s in a 108s session HAR). Now it calls Nominatim directly (no key; usage policy honored via the page Referer) and drops the unsupported custom User-Agent header (browsers ignore it). Place names still resolve identically; the per-report stagger + cacheKey memo are unchanged. Returning operators must evict the stale app.js. // v81 (Jun 2026): Web Dashboard interaction-audit remediation (D1-D7). D1: a building card on the operation dashboard now opens a VISIBLE Building Console - openBuildingConsole reparents #detail-panel to <body> (like selectReport; it was opening inside the hidden #cc-ops-overlay container) + the deep-link hash is route-first (#/operations/{id};building={bid}, was a malformed prepend). D2: #detail-panel closes on Escape (topmost-first, not when its child reason/compare modal is open) + focus moves into the panel on open and restores to the prior element on close. D3: an op-map marker click retains the operation id (routes #/incidents;op={id}?incident={rid}, was a bare openIncident that dropped scope). D4: Undo-claim now asks for confirmation, disables the button during the request, and defers the success redirect ~1.8s so the toast is readable. D5: the in-page panels (analytics/predictions/deletions/moderation) + transient modal overlays are torn down on EVERY route change (router.hideAll -> window.__ccCloseTransientOverlays), so none can orphan onto the next route. D6: NEW shared window.withBusy(btn, fn) double-submit guard (disables the control + shows an inline spinner for buttons, re-entrant-safe; for <select>/<input> it only disables so options survive) applied to the wizard Launch, Settings save-profile/password/role-change/active-toggle/delete-user/org-branding, and the duplicate Merge/Not/Remove/Make-primary/Unmerge-all controls. D7: an Export opened from an operation that lost its scope now shows a warning banner instead of silently exporting the GLOBAL dataset. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/cc-operations.js/cc-settings.js/cc-wizard.js/cc-exports.js/router.js/crisp-building-card.js + styles.css. // v80 (Jun 2026): operation Buildings worklist - local scroll, ~5 visible, lazy-load. The operation-dashboard "Buildings" worklist (#cco-bld) rendered EVERY affected building as a full card in a 360px box, so an op with many buildings crammed ~8 cards into the map-height column (no breathing room) or pushed the panel past the map. Now the worklist (1) is a LOCAL scroll height-matched to the Operation Map (max-height:360px from .cco-wl, both 360px), (2) shows ~5 de-congested cards at a time (#cco-bld .bic min-height:58px + gap:8px → ~5.5 fit the 360px viewport; overscroll-behavior:contain keeps the page from scrolling past the list), and (3) LAZY-LOADS the rest: CrispBuildingCard.renderInto gained an opts.pageSize window (renderOpBuildings passes 8) that renders the first page and appends the next as the operator scrolls within 80px of the bottom (a prior render's scroll listener is dropped first, so re-renders don't stack). The shared card's non-lazy path (Global home Building Intelligence, no pageSize) is unchanged. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale cc-operations.js/crisp-building-card.js + styles.css. // v79 (Jun 2026): session resilience across access-token expiry - the dashboard no longer "goes numb / bounces to home" after ~30 min. ROOT CAUSE: ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=30; the global fetch wrapper HARD-logged-out on the FIRST 401 (wiped crisp_token + crisp_user → redirect to login; the router's canRoute, reading the now-missing crisp_user role, then bounced EVERY click to home). The only safety net was one fragile 25-min setInterval (no reactive refresh; throttled in backgrounded tabs). FIX: on a 401 for an /api call the wrapper now does a TRANSPARENT /auth/refresh (using crisp_refresh, shared in-flight so concurrent 401s trigger ONE refresh) and RETRIES the request once; it only hard-logs-out if the refresh itself fails (or there's no refresh token). The /auth/* endpoints are excluded (no refresh loop); the retry is marked so a still-401 retry logs out cleanly (no infinite loop). Plus the proactive refresh now runs every 10 min AND on visibilitychange (when a backgrounded tab refocuses), so a throttled timer can't let the token lapse. Net: an operator working a long shift keeps their session silently; the access token rotating in the background is invisible. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v78 (Jun 2026): duplicate "Merge all" - one click, group-aware, honest counts. (1) NEW prominent "Merge all (N)" button on the Incidents "Potential Duplicates" panel collapses EVERY level (High+Medium+Low) in ONE click (confidence=ALL), beside the existing per-level buttons. (2) Backend duplicate-merge is now GROUP-AWARE (union-find over the candidate pairs + existing confirmed stars): a whole duplicate cluster/chain collapses under ONE primary in a single pass - never pair-by-pair, no stragglers left needing another click; an existing primary in a cluster is reused (extends its star) instead of forking. (3) The surviving PRIMARY is the report that LANDED FIRST (the original), ties broken toward the MOST-COMPLETE report (_rdd_info_score = media + description + verified + building + crisis/damage/infra/service fields). (4) ROOT-CAUSE FIX for "Merge all does nothing": _rdd_candidate_pairs (which backs BOTH the summary counts AND the merge) now EXCLUDES reports already collapsed under a primary - previously it counted phantom pairs between already-merged reports, so the panel showed e.g. "140 Potential Duplicates" that could never be merged and the count never dropped. The summary now reflects only genuinely-mergeable pairs (the panel hides at 0). Fully reversible (Unmerge). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v77 (Jun 2026): the feed-truncation banner ("Feed list shows the newest 500 of N reports …") is now a TRANSIENT ~5s message, not a persistent top-of-page bar. It was pinned to the top of <body> and driven by the global reports poll, so it lingered across every route (even the /operations registry + home, where it's irrelevant) and re-appeared on every full-refresh. Now _showTruncationBanner shows it ONCE per truncation episode (guarded by _truncShown) and auto-dismisses after 5s - consistent with the other informational banners. _truncShown is reset when the shortfall resolves and on every scope change (setOperationScope), so each newly-entered truncated scope shows it once. The × close + the counts/map-reflect-all semantics are unchanged. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v76 (Jun 2026): Notification AGE GATE - stop historical reports replaying as individual toasts on navigation. ROOT CAUSE (the v74 show-once fix did not cover this): _addNotification toasts any report that is NEW to the working-set + not in _seenIds, with NO check on the report's AGE. Opening an Operation (setOperationScope -> scoped full-refresh -> _replaceReportData evicts knownIds -> the op's hours-old reports, never in the initial global window, are "new") fired a center-screen "NEW INCIDENT REPORTED" toast for reports created hours ago. FIX: in _addNotification, after the durable bell-write (_seenIds + _notifCenterAdd + _renderNotifications) and the Category-C return, an AGE GATE - only reports CREATED within _REALTIME_WINDOW_MS (5 min) of now flash an individual toast / engage burst; older reports land SILENTLY in the Notification Center (unread, reviewable) and never pop a card. Missing/unparseable server_created_at => treated as real-time (never drop a genuine arrival); client_report_id is NOT a bypass (nearly every report has one). Age - not seen-state - is the discriminator (an id evicted from the 1000-cap _seenIds and reloaded via a scope switch is still old => still no re-toast). Plus: a scope full-refresh that surfaces a BACKLOG of >= _BACKLOG_BANNER_MIN (3) silent historical reports shows ONE lightweight "since your last visit · +N new reports received while you were away" banner (auto-dismiss ~5s) via _replaceReportData, instead of N pop-ups. Real-time arrivals still toast normally; all unseen reports remain in the bell. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v75 (Jun 2026): Active Operations scalability - the home rail no longer renders EVERY operation as a tall full-width stat card (50 ops = a ~4,000px scroll wall with no triage). (1) HOME RAIL = a worst-first TOP-N (6) shortlist of COMPACT one-line rows (health dot + name/place + Critical, no inline SVG map / KPI strip / trend) under a PORTFOLIO SUMMARY bar (N live · X critical-state · Y rising · Z stable · unattended · total critical reports) whose chips deep-link into the filtered registry; the orphan-critical "no operation" CTA is now a slim one-line alert (was a full card); "Start New" moved into the band header ("+ New"); a "+ N more · View all N" footer routes the long tail to the registry. (2) /operations = the scalable REGISTRY: search (name/place) + status segment (Live/Ended/All) + health filter chips (Critical/Rising/Stable/Unattended) + sort (worst-first / recent / name) + a density toggle (comfortable full card <-> compact row, persisted) + windowing (show 30, Load more) - so 50-500 operations scan without a wall. (3) CrispOpCard gains a reusable `compact` variant + a `presorted` render flag. Backend GET /operations gains optional status/order(priority)/limit/offset params + an X-Total-Count header (must-have #12); all default to the prior behaviour so existing callers are unchanged. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale cc-home.js/cc-operations.js + styles.css. // v74 (Jun 2026): Notification experience redesign - eliminate replay / analyst fatigue. ROOT CAUSE fixed: the notify path left NO durable "displayed" marker, so an operation-scope full-refresh (setOperationScope -> _replaceReportData) that evicts knownIds made already-seen reports look new and re-flash on every Home/Operations/Incidents navigation, even hours later. (1) SHOW-ONCE: _addNotification now writes the report id into the persisted _seenIds ledger AT NOTIFY TIME (on the confirmed-new branch, after dedup), so the poll's producer gate (_applyReportData) suppresses every future re-delivery - no replay on route change / scope switch / refresh. (2) DURABLE NOTIFICATION CENTER: the bell is backed by a persisted, per-operator _notifCenter (crisp_notif_center_<uid>) holding READ + UNREAD history (survives refresh; replaces the transient _unseenReports that was wiped every reload); badge = UNREAD count; "Mark all read" keeps history, "Clear" purges read items. Unread / Earlier sections. (3) SESSION SUMMARY: one "Since your last visit: +N reports - +M critical - across K operations" banner per BROWSER SESSION (sessionStorage guard, never on route change), measured against a per-operator last-visit watermark (crisp_last_visit_<uid>, advanced on beforeunload); also recorded in the center. (4) CATEGORIES: A Informational (toast ~5s, never repeat), B Important = CRITICAL severity (toast 5s + stays highlighted in the center until read), C Urgent = persistent-until-acknowledged red banner (window.crispUrgentBroadcast; NO automatic producer - the audit confirmed nothing in the report path is urgent). (5) Toast auto-dismiss standardized 6s -> ~5s. The single global manager already existed (no per-page producers); cc-home/cc-operations untouched. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/crisp-shell.js + styles.css. // v73 (Jun 2026): Building Intelligence P0 - Buildings are now a PRIMARY operational object (Global -> Operations -> Buildings -> Reports), surfaced over the existing building engine (no new tables / migration / route / cluster entity). (1) The Crisis Intelligence home gains a "Building Intelligence" section ranking buildings by operational importance (GET /buildings?order_by=humanitarian_priority) via a shared CrispBuildingCard - report volume stays visible alongside (corroboration is signal). (2) The operation dashboard worklist gains a Reports|Buildings toggle with BUILDINGS as the default tab (the op's affected buildings, ranked by priority); the Reports worklist is one click away. (3) The Building Console (= Building Details, reached via the ;building= overlay) gains a per-building Duplicates section (GET /reports/duplicate-summary?building_id= + Merge-All High/Medium, reusing the shipped engine - never a parallel scorer) and a Health "why" breakdown (the 5 component scores x their published weights = humanitarian_priority). (4) Operator-facing "Cluster" wording -> "Building" (breadcrumb shows the building name; "Open Building Details"); wire names (cluster_count etc.) UNCHANGED so analytics/integrations don't break. Backend: _rdd_candidate_pairs gains a building_id scope; /duplicate-summary + /duplicate-merge gain a building_id passthrough; BuildingSummary gains additive critical_report_count / responder_count / duplicate_group_count (cheap per-page grouped queries, no N+1). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/cc-home.js/cc-operations.js + pick up the new crisp-building-card.js. // v72 (Jun 2026): Duplicate Management - confirmed duplicates now COLLAPSE under their primary instead of cluttering the feed. A report an analyst confirms as a duplicate is HIDDEN from the default feed + the map (still reachable by id + via ?include_duplicates=true; nothing deleted; fully reversible via Undo / Unmerge / Make-primary). The primary report wears a "🔗 N duplicate reports merged" badge in the feed and its map pin shows the "N reports" count (one pin per incident, no overlapping duplicate pins). The report-detail duplicate section is now "Related Duplicate Reports" (View / Switch / Remove-from-group / Unmerge-all / Make-primary) plus a WHITE-BOX "why" breakdown (Same building / Within 1h / Similar image / Similar description / Same reporter - the documented scorer weights, no black box). The Incidents context-banner dual count is now "X incidents · Y reports" (incidents = duplicates collapsed; reports = full volume incl. corroboration). NEW Incidents-page "Potential Duplicates" panel (High/Medium/Low/Total + "Merge All High/Medium/Low" + "Review Individually") backed by GET /reports/duplicate-summary + POST /reports/duplicate-merge (analyst-only; never auto-merges). /analytics/summary gains additive incidents + reports counts. A new report arriving in a building that ALREADY has a visible incident notifies as "Existing Incident Updated (+1 corroborating report)" instead of "New Incident". NO new tables / migration / routes / cluster entity - the whole feature rides the existing report_duplicate_decisions relationship (the primary report IS the operational incident). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v71 (Jun 2026): on the INCIDENTS page, the redundant shell operation breadcrumb bar ("CRISP / Operations / {name} · Exit to global ✕", #cgn-context-banner) is now HIDDEN - the in-feed context banner (#queue-banner) already names the operation + carries a "Global" exit. Route-scoped CSS (body.crisp-op-scoped[data-route="/incidents"] #cgn-context-banner{display:none}); the bar STAYS on /operations/{id} where it's the primary op chrome, and the colored nav accent + GLOBAL/OP scope chip remain (so the shell never reads GLOBAL while the feed reads OPERATION). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale crisp-shell.js. // v70 (Jun 2026): tightened the operation context banner (#queue-banner, _renderContextBanner). The operation NAME is now merged into the bold header line ("OPERATION · {name}", single-line + ellipsised) instead of buried in a verbose 2-line sub that overflowed + truncated ("Bangalore-Wildfire · only this operation · 1 cluster · 2..."); the redundant "only this operation" filler is dropped and the sub is now just "{region} · N clusters · M incidents". The render no longer emits a dangling " · " when the sub is empty. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js + styles.css. // v69 (Jun 2026): incident-open routing is now CALLER-CONTEXT aware (CrispNav.openIncident). Clicking an incident that belongs to an operation while ON the Incidents page (#/incidents, global OR op-scoped) no longer EJECTS to that operation's dashboard (/operations/{id}) - it STAYS on the Incidents page and op-scopes the feed IN PLACE (#/incidents;op={opId}?incident={id}), so the feed header names the operation and the detail opens there. Opening from the operation dashboard's own surfaces still keeps the op-dashboard context; home/notification entry points are unchanged. (router.buildHash exposed on window.__crispRouter.) Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale crisp-nav.js/router.js. // v68 (Jun 2026): Incident Intelligence P2-P4. P2: the Clusters feed cards open the Cluster View (the existing Building Console, extended with a breadcrumb + assigned-operation chip); a building-backed cluster card gets an "open cluster" button; the report-detail breadcrumb gains a CLUSTER segment (Operation/Global -> Cluster -> Incident) so opening a report from a cluster keeps context; cluster expand-state persists across feed re-renders. P3: within-cluster duplicate surfacing in the report detail ("Possible duplicates" section) - confidence chips (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW) from GET /reports/{id}/duplicates (time + category + fuzzy description + pHash + device), with analyst controls Confirm / Not-duplicate / Set-primary / Undo (POST /reports/{id}/duplicate-decision; backend report_duplicate_decisions table, migration 0054; the scorer honors stored decisions). P4: additive "N clusters - M incidents" dual count in the incident context banner, backed by a new additive cluster_count in /analytics/summary (distinct active buildings + building-less singletons); per-report needs-review/dispatch counts, exports + notifications UNCHANGED. ("Move to another cluster" control + the server-side /reports/clusters scale endpoint + promoting Clusters to the default view are deferred - gated on real-data validation.) Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v67 (Jun 2026): Incident Intelligence P1 - opt-in "Clusters" feed view. A 3rd feed view-mode button (Queue / Clusters / Tree; default Queue) groups reports into Building/Location incident clusters so the analyst sees ONE operational problem, not N report cards. Cluster key precedence: building_id -> h3 cell (~175m, now in the location payload) -> the report itself (singleton), so nothing ever disappears. Clusters render as collapsible cards (name + report_count + critical + new-24h + last-activity), collapsed by default; expanding shows the reports as evidence (reused createIncidentCard); clicking a report opens its detail. Read-time aggregation over the loaded working set (server-side /reports/clusters at 500k scale is deferred). Backend: LocationResponse now serializes h3_idx (additive). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v66 (Jun 2026): Incidents load-order / operation-context integrity - root-cause fix for the "flash of GLOBAL incidents" on Operation → Incident navigation. (1) The /incidents dispatch now determines operation CONTEXT and calls setOperationScope() BEFORE showIncidents() reveals the view (was the reverse - revealed the stale global #report-feed-list DOM first). (2) setOperationScope() clears the prior set, sets a `_scopeLoading` flag, and REPAINTS the feed to a scope-named "Loading Operation Incidents…" state immediately (so nothing stale flashes before the view is revealed). renderFeed() shows that loading state while the LIST fetch is in flight (gated on `_scopeLoading`, which is cleared ONLY when the LIST fetchReports applies data - NOT by the by-id lazy fetch, so the loading state isn't ended by the single auto-opened incident). (3) fetchReports() captures the scope at request time and DISCARDS a response whose scope changed mid-flight (kills the in-flight-global-poll-applies-after-scope-change flash) → a single correct render. (4) Cold boot / refresh of #/incidents;op=X reads the scope from the hash before the first fetch + skips the stale global localStorage cache, so the FIRST load is scoped (no global fetch+render). (5) The context banner already renders before the list (names the operation). (6) Instrumentation: window.__crispRouteTrace (enable via localStorage.crisp_nav_trace='1') logs dispatch → setOperationScope → dataset loaded → incident auto-opened. Nav-path audit confirmed all incident-open paths already preserve op context. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/router.js/crisp-nav.js. // v65 (Jun 2026): account-dropdown cleanup. (1) The "Crisis Intelligence" launcher (#cc-home-launch, injected by cc-home.js) is HIDDEN when already on the Crisis Intelligence home page (route '/') and shown elsewhere - it's only a way back home; re-evaluated on every route change (hashchange). (2) Fixed duplicate "Account settings" / "Organisation settings" entries: cc-settings.js no longer injects its own (non-router) copies - the canonical STATIC, router-driven #btn-account-settings (->/users) + #btn-org-settings (->/org) in index.html are the single source (a leftover from the header-consolidation that added the static items without removing the injected ones). openOverlay + window.openAccountSettings/openOrgSettings unchanged (still back the routes). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale cc-home.js/cc-settings.js. // v64 (Jun 2026): robust auto-scroll-to-selected-incident on navigation. When an incident is opened (op-worklist click / deep-link / search) the feed now reliably scrolls it into view + highlights it even in a long, grouped, scrollable list. Three obstacles that re-apply on every render are handled: (1) progressive disclosure (cards past index 50 are display:none) now keeps the SELECTED card within the revealed window (_applyProgressiveReveal is selection-aware); (2) a default-COLLAPSED queue section (HELP SENT / CLOSED) that holds the selected card renders EXPANDED without mutating the operator's saved collapse preference (createQueueSection); (3) renderFeed rebuilds #report-feed-list (resetting scrollTop) - CrispNav now retries per-frame until the card is laid out, re-asserts the scroll across re-renders for a ~2.5s settling window (instant snap on re-assert, smooth on first reveal), and never yanks the operator back once THEY scroll (scrollTop>8 guard). scrollIntoView centers the card (block:center). Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/crisp-nav.js. // v63 (Jun 2026): operation-dashboard incident UX. (1) The action button "Open full incident feed" is renamed "Open Incident Feed". (2) Clicking an incident row in the operation dashboard's "Operation incidents" worklist now LEAVES the operation dashboard for the full Incident Feed page SCOPED to that operation with the report SELECTED (#/incidents;op={opId}?incident={id}) - the feed list renders on the LEFT with that row highlighted + scrolled into view, and the detail report opens on the RIGHT - instead of opening the detail inline over the operation dashboard. Routed through the canonical deep-link path (router.dispatch -> setOperationScope(opId) -> CrispNav.restoreFromHash -> selectReport + markSelected), so it is deep-linkable + survives refresh/Back/Forward. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/cc-operations.js. // v62 (Jun 2026): the irreversible report-purge (Pending Deletions -> "Purge all" / "Purge expired") no longer prompts for a shared static admin key via window.prompt. It now uses per-operator step-up ("sudo") auth: a new in-app modal collects the operator's authenticator (TOTP) code - or their account password if no MFA is enrolled - POSTs it to /auth/step-up (which verifies + issues a short-lived ~10-min step-up token, audited STEP_UP_OK/FAILED), and the purge endpoints require that token via an X-Step-Up header (SUPER_ADMIN JWT still required on top). The token is cached in sessionStorage for its window so the operator is asked only ONCE per ~10 min; a wrong code re-prompts in place (bounded) and an expired token re-confirms once - neither logs the operator out (these calls bypass the global 401->logout interceptor). The old CRISP_ADMIN_KEY env requirement is retired (verify_admin_key is now a no-op shim) + X-Step-Up added to the CORS allow-list. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js. // v61 (Jun 2026): header declutter - Organisation / Users / Account removed from the primary nav (crisp-shell) and moved into the account-chip dropdown as "Account settings" (all users) + admin-gated "User Management" / "Organisation Settings", all router-driven (deep-linkable). Primary nav is now operational-only: Incidents · Exports · Crisis Forms. The old cc-crisis account-dropdown "Crisis Forms" injection (redundant + non-router) was removed - Crisis Forms is reached via its nav button / op-dashboard / #/reporting. Returning operators must evict the precached index.html + stale app.js/crisp-shell.js/cc-crisis.js. // v60 (Jun 2026): pre-rollout Phase 1-5 remediation. Counts: ONE canonical contract (Critical = open CRITICAL everywhere; needs_review = open & not-yet-accepted, closing the REJECTED-leak; pending-verification open-only) across the server summary + operations rollup + client KPI strip/pill/home card; op-card Critical no longer inflated by closed reports. Operations: op switcher refetches fresh (ENDED ops drop out, new ones appear); a deleted/unknown op shows a "not found" state (not a phantom GREEN dashboard) + ENDED ops show READ-ONLY; the shell scope chip syncs on the op-scoped feed; chip filters